# Noise list for searching dotfiles under $HOME. Used by rgdot() in
# ~/.zsh/functions.zsh. gitignore syntax. Survives -u/--no-ignore because it is
# passed with --ignore-file rather than found on disk.
#
# Two gotchas:
#
# 1. Every multi-segment pattern needs a leading `**/`. A pattern containing a
#    slash is anchored, and with --ignore-file the anchor is your *current
#    working directory*, not the search root. Written bare, `.local/share/mise/`
#    silently matches nothing. Single-name patterns like `.asdf/` are already
#    unanchored and match at any depth, so they need no prefix.
#
# 2. Nothing here can exclude a path that rgdot passes as a root. Ignore rules
#    apply only *below* a root, and an explicitly named file is always searched.
#    Whole top-level entries are dropped by the glob in rgdot(); this file
#    handles everything deeper.
#
#    So a name belongs here only if it can occur *nested*. Entries that exist
#    solely at the top level (.asdf, .rustup, .pry.d, .Trash) live in rgdot's
#    glob and nowhere else - listing them here would look protective but do
#    nothing. The few names in both lists are there because they genuinely nest.

# Language runtimes and toolchain installs
**/.local/share/mise/
**/.local/share/rtx/
**/.cargo/registry/
**/.cargo/git/

# Package-manager caches
.npm/
.yarn/
.gem/
.bundle/
.cache/

# Installed third-party code and caches
**/.local/share/nvim*/
**/.local/share/ruby-advisory-db/
**/.local/pipx/
**/.claude/plugins/cache/
**/.codex/plugins/cache/
**/.codex/.tmp/

# Editor scratch space
**/.cursor/worktrees/
**/.cursor/extensions/
**/.vscode/extensions/

# Agent transcripts - mostly noise. ~/.claude/history.jsonl is
# deliberately NOT covered: it sits directly in .claude/, not under projects/,
# and it is the durable log of typed prompts that outlives transcript pruning.
**/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl
**/.codex/sessions/**/*.jsonl

# nvim undo binary blobs
**/nvim*/undo/

# Log and archive noise
*.log
*.log.*
*.tar
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.zip

# Shell/REPL history. Deliberately not a bare `*history*`: that would also drop
# ~/.claude/history.jsonl. Requiring the underscore is what spares it.
*_history*
*lesshst
*wget-hsts
